{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F2ts9ftGwAC2cdc5gwPwKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to expand detailed predicted data for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"median\" tier assumptions. Each prediction must include a result_rationale explaining why this result would occur under the median tier.\n\nLet me carefully go through each experiment and predict results consistent with the median tier definition:\n\nMedian tier key characteristics:\n- Real contamination moderate: fitted c_n median ∈ [0.3, 0.8)\n- G-MFRM converges but may need tuning (R̂ ≤ 1.10, ESS ≥ 100)\n\n\n- G-MFRM shows competitive performance against naive baselines with only marginal improvements over stronger competitors\n- The e_i pipeline functions adequately though one source contributes minimally to the overall signal\n- Error propagation introduces modest sensitivity with degradation in the 5-15% range\n- Model rankings shift slightly with only 1-2 position changes while the top-5 remains largely consistent\n- ConStat validation shows moderate correlation strength between 0.4 and 0.7\n\nNow I'm establishing the specific metric ranges for these predictions: real contamination levels between 0.3 and 0.8, Kendall tau values for G-MFRM between 0.84 and 0.9, and delta tau measurements against the best baseline.\n\nLooking at the broader experimental metrics, I see RMSE improvements of 10-30% over sequential approaches, convergence diagnostics showing Rhat values near 1.0-1.1 and effective sample sizes between 100-250, synthetic recovery RMSE around 0.15-0.3, rank position changes limited to 1-3 spots, and the minimum judge count needed for significant gains falling between 4-6. Now I'm starting to review the individual experiments, beginning with the multi-judge data collection phase.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12445,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12445},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9c2bc3-9f18-4e08-9e81-79982f6c114b","uuid":"aaf3f572-f1bd-4f6b-bbe1-ddaabbce52bb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01F2ts9ftGwAC2cdc5gwPwKe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Tier B narrative. Real contamination is detectable but moderate (c_n median ~0.5).\n  G-MFRM ranking improvement over best baselines is statistically significant but practically modest (+2-3pp Kendall-τ).\n  Pivot primary contribution to diagnostic/interpretability outputs: per-model c_n as training data audit tool,\n  per-item e_i for item retirement decisions, per-judge d_j for judge selection guidance.\n  Lead argument: 'Sequential methods provide no visibility into whether corrections are needed —\n  G-MFRM provides both correction and diagnosis.' Forward-looking: as contamination grows, joint estimation becomes critical.\n  May need exp-010 (WildBench) to strengthen empirical package with a third benchmark.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: multi_judge_data_collection\n    plan_id: exp-001\n    description: >\n      Collect multi-judge evaluation data on MT-Bench and Arena-Hard using 8 judges.\n      20+ target models evaluated with position swap.\n    expected_results:\n      num_judges: 8\n      num_target_models: 22\n      benchmarks: [\"MT-Bench\", \"Arena-Hard\"]\n      total_judgments_mt_bench: 28160  # 22 models × 80 items × 8 judges × 2 positions\n      total_judgments_arena_hard: 35200  # 22 models × 100 items × 8 judges × 2 positions\n      position_bias_detected_judges: 3\n      api_cost_usd: 820\n      gpu_hours_used: 118\n      missing_data_pct: 2.1\n      inter_judge_agreement_fleiss_kappa: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下，8个judge的评分会展现出中等程度的一致性（Fleiss κ~0.38），反映了judge之间severity差异的真实存在。\n      22个target model覆盖了从GPT-5.5到开源7B模型的能力梯度，确保contamination susceptibility的变异性。\n      Position bias在3个judge上显著（主要是较小的开源judge），这为d_j估计提供了必要的judge间变异。\n      缺失数据约2%来自API超时和vLLM偶发OOM，在可接受范围内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Judge × Benchmark Data Collection Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"MT-Bench Items\", \"Arena-Hard Items\", \"Position Swap\", \"Missing %\", \"Mean Score\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.82\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.45\"]\n          - [\"Claude Sonnet 4.6\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.61\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"1.8%\", \"7.28\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"2.5%\", \"7.15\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3.6-27B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"4.2%\", \"6.93\"]\n          - [\"Llama 4 Maverick\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"3.1%\", \"7.05\"]\n          - [\"Gemma3-27B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"2.8%\", \"6.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: Judge score distribution heatmap (judge × target model), showing systematic severity differences across judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据收集本身不直接验证claim，但数据质量决定了后续实验的上限。\n      Judge间score分布差异（mean range: 6.88–7.82）确认了judge severity变异的存在，为d_j估计提供信号。\n      中等的inter-judge agreement (κ~0.38) 意味着judge bias correction有实际意义。\n\n  - name: item_exposure_estimation\n    plan_id: exp-002\n    description: >\n      三源pipeline估计per-item exposure e_i。Primary source: 原始vs改写变体的performance gap；\n      Temporal: pre/post-cutoff变体gap；LogProber: token logprob memorization scores。\n      加权组合后用ConStat per-model delta做外部验证。\n    expected_results:\n      num_items_mt_bench: 80\n      num_items_arena_hard: 100\n      reference_variants_created: 180\n      primary_source_coverage: 1.0\n      temporal_source_coverage: 0.45\n      logprober_source_coverage: 0.55\n      composite_e_i_mean: 0.32\n      composite_e_i_std: 0.21\n      composite_e_i_range: [0.0, 0.82]\n      high_exposure_items_pct: 18.0  # e_i > 0.5\n      primary_temporal_correlation: 0.58\n      primary_logprober_correlation: 0.41\n      weighted_composite_internal_consistency_alpha: 0.62\n      constat_cn_vs_gmfrm_cn_spearman: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设real contamination moderate，因此e_i分布右偏但不极端：大部分items（~82%）的e_i < 0.5，\n      仅少数items（~18%）有明显的contamination exposure。这与\"contamination exists but is moderate\"一致。\n      Primary source（performance gap）覆盖率100%且信号最强；temporal source覆盖率有限（仅45%的items有\n      pre/post-cutoff变体），但与primary的相关性中等（r=0.58）。LogProber覆盖率55%（仅有logprob API的模型），\n      且与primary相关性较弱（r=0.41）——这是median档的关键特征之一：\"one source contributes little\"。\n      内部一致性α=0.62反映了三源信号的中等coherence，足以构建可用的composite但不overwhelming。\n      ConStat验证ρ=0.52落在[0.4, 0.7)范围内，表明fitted c_n与外部contamination measure有中等agreement。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Exposure Indicator Source Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"Coverage\", \"Mean e_i\", \"Std\", \"Correlation w/ Composite\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Primary (performance gap)\", \"100%\", \"0.30\", \"0.22\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"Temporal (pre/post cutoff)\", \"45%\", \"0.35\", \"0.25\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"LogProber (logprob)\", \"55%\", \"0.28\", \"0.19\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Composite\", \"100%\", \"0.32\", \"0.21\", \"1.00\"]\n      - name: \"Table S2: High-Exposure Items (e_i > 0.5)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Item ID\", \"e_i\", \"Primary\", \"Temporal\", \"LogProber\", \"Category\"]\n        note: \"~32 items total (18% of 180). Concentrated in coding and math categories.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2(a): e_i histogram across all items, showing right-skewed distribution with mode near 0.15 and tail to 0.82.\"\n      - \"Fig 2(b): Source-pair scatter plots (primary vs temporal, primary vs LogProber) with regression lines.\"\n      - \"Fig S2: Per-benchmark e_i distribution comparison (MT-Bench vs Arena-Hard).\"\n    analysis: >\n      e_i pipeline产生合理的exposure estimates，但LogProber贡献有限。这意味着在ablation（exp-007）中，\n      去除LogProber对composite质量影响较小，2/3 sources sufficient。\n      MT-Bench的coding/math items的e_i系统性高于reasoning/writing items，\n      与contamination通过training data leakage的机制一致。\n      Arena-Hard的e_i整体略低于MT-Bench，可能因Arena-Hard更新更频繁、泄露窗口更短。\n\n  - name: gmfrm_real_data_fit\n    plan_id: exp-003\n    description: >\n      在exp-001/002的real data上拟合G-MFRM三阶段pipeline。\n      Stage 1: MFRM估计(θ,b,d)。Stage 2: 固定exp-002的e_i。Stage 3: Joint gated model。\n      输出fair scores θ̂并与Chatbot Arena Elo对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # Convergence\n      stage1_max_rhat: 1.02\n      stage1_min_ess: 380\n      stage3_max_rhat: 1.07\n      stage3_min_ess: 142\n      stage3_divergent_transitions: 12\n      # Parameters\n      theta_range: [-1.8, 2.1]\n      d_j_range: [-0.62, 0.48]\n      d_j_std: 0.31\n      c_n_median: 0.48\n      c_n_mean: 0.54\n      c_n_range: [0.05, 1.35]\n      c_n_gt_0_3_count: 13  # out of 22 models\n      c_n_gt_0_8_count: 4\n      # Fit quality\n      kendall_tau_arena_mt_bench: 0.87\n      kendall_tau_arena_arena_hard: 0.86\n      spearman_rho_arena_mt_bench: 0.91\n      spearman_rho_arena_arena_hard: 0.90\n      # Graceful degradation check\n      arena_hard_subset_low_contamination_tau_gmfrm: 0.88\n      arena_hard_subset_low_contamination_tau_mfrm: 0.87\n      runtime_seconds: 8400\n      mcmc_warmup: 2000\n      mcmc_samples: 4000\n      mcmc_chains: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心特征在此实验集中体现。c_n median=0.48落在[0.3, 0.8)区间，\n      接近mvp_001的weak contamination而非mvp_003的strong contamination。\n      22个模型中13个有c_n > 0.3（moderate），仅4个有c_n > 0.8（heavy），\n      说明contamination普遍存在但幅度有限。\n      Stage 3收敛需要调优：R̂=1.07（≤1.10但不ideal）、ESS=142（≥100但远低于mvp_003的224），\n      12个divergent transitions提示geometry有困难但未破坏inference。\n      这是因为moderate contamination意味着c_n的posterior更diffuse（数据对c_n的约束力较弱），\n      MCMC更难探索。Kendall-τ=0.87落在[0.84, 0.9]范围，比raw average显著提升但不dramatic。\n      低contamination子集上G-MFRM与MFRM几乎无差异（0.88 vs 0.87），确认graceful degradation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: G-MFRM Convergence Diagnostics\"\n        columns: [\"Parameter Group\", \"Max R̂\", \"Min ESS\", \"Mean ESS\", \"Divergent Transitions\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"θ (model ability)\", \"1.03\", \"285\", \"420\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"b (item difficulty)\", \"1.02\", \"310\", \"465\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"d (judge severity)\", \"1.02\", \"340\", \"490\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"c (contamination)\", \"1.07\", \"142\", \"215\", \"12\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4: Per-Model Parameter Estimates (sorted by θ̂)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"θ̂ (fair)\", \"θ_raw\", \"c_n\", \"c_n 95%CI\", \"Rank_fair\", \"Rank_raw\", \"Δ Rank\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"1.95\", \"2.08\", \"0.72\", \"[0.38, 1.12]\", \"1\", \"1\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"1.82\", \"1.85\", \"0.21\", \"[0.03, 0.52]\", \"2\", \"3\", \"+1\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", \"1.71\", \"1.92\", \"1.15\", \"[0.68, 1.35]\", \"3\", \"2\", \"-1\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", \"1.45\", \"1.58\", \"0.65\", \"[0.31, 1.02]\", \"5\", \"4\", \"-1\"]\n          - [\"Model-X-70B\", \"0.85\", \"1.10\", \"1.28\", \"[0.85, 1.35]\", \"10\", \"7\", \"-3\"]\n          - [\"Small-7B-Chat\", \"-1.52\", \"-1.48\", \"0.08\", \"[0.01, 0.28]\", \"22\", \"22\", \"0\"]\n      - name: \"Table S3: Per-Judge Severity Estimates\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"d_j\", \"d_j 95%CI\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"-0.15\", \"[-0.32, 0.02]\", \"Slightly lenient\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"0.08\", \"[-0.10, 0.25]\", \"Near neutral\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3.6-27B\", \"0.48\", \"[0.28, 0.68]\", \"Most severe\"]\n          - [\"Llama 4 Maverick\", \"-0.62\", \"[-0.85, -0.40]\", \"Most lenient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Scatter plot of θ̂_fair vs Chatbot Arena Elo, colored by c_n magnitude. High-c_n models pulled downward relative to raw scores.\"\n      - \"Fig 4: c_n posterior density plots for all 22 models, ordered by posterior median. Shows moderate contamination landscape.\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Trace plots for c_n of 4 highest-contamination models, showing adequate mixing despite slower convergence.\"\n      - \"Fig S4: θ̂_raw vs θ̂_fair with identity line; deviations annotated with model names.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM成功拟合real data，收敛可接受但不完美（c_n的ESS偏低）。\n      c_n median=0.48确认了median档预期：contamination存在且可量化，但幅度moderate。\n      关键发现：4个模型（DeepSeek-V4-Pro, Qwen3-235B-A22B, Model-X-70B, 另一个）的c_n > 0.8，\n      这些模型的fair score显著低于raw score，产生了有意义的rank changes。\n      但top-5整体稳定（仅1-2个位置变动），限制了ranking correction的headline impact。\n      Per-judge d_j range（-0.62 to 0.48）确认judge severity差异显著，\n      为\"judge selection guidance\"这一diagnostic贡献提供了直接证据。\n\n  - name: baseline_comparison\n    plan_id: exp-004\n    description: >\n      G-MFRM vs 8条baselines在相同数据上对比。\n      包含rank change analysis：具体哪些模型换位、换多少位、top-k稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      # Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena (MT-Bench)\n      tau_raw_average: 0.79\n      tau_mfrm_only: 0.82\n      tau_sequential: 0.84\n      tau_cyclicjudge: 0.83\n      tau_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.85\n      tau_dcr_factor: 0.81\n      tau_uda: 0.84\n      tau_pref_leakage_cal: 0.82\n      tau_gmfrm: 0.87\n      # Spearman-ρ with Chatbot Arena (MT-Bench)\n      rho_raw_average: 0.83\n      rho_mfrm_only: 0.86\n      rho_sequential: 0.88\n      rho_cyclicjudge: 0.87\n      rho_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.89\n      rho_dcr_factor: 0.85\n      rho_uda: 0.88\n      rho_pref_leakage_cal: 0.86\n      rho_gmfrm: 0.91\n      # Arena-Hard results similar pattern\n      tau_gmfrm_arena_hard: 0.86\n      tau_best_baseline_arena_hard: 0.84\n      # Δτ vs best baseline\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_mt_bench: 0.02\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_arena_hard: 0.02\n      # Statistical significance\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_cyclicjudge_discard_p: 0.073\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_sequential_p: 0.018\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_raw_p: 0.001\n      # Rank change analysis\n      rank_changes_ge2_positions: 2\n      top5_stability_raw_vs_gmfrm: \"4/5 same\"\n      top10_stability_raw_vs_gmfrm: \"7/10 same\"\n      max_rank_change_model: \"Model-X-70B\"\n      max_rank_change_positions: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心tension在此实验体现：G-MFRM beats all baselines但margin modest。\n      Δτ=+0.02 vs CyclicJudge+discard（best baseline），p=0.073——borderline significant。\n      这是因为moderate contamination意味着contamination correction的marginal value有限：\n      CyclicJudge+discard已经通过丢弃high-exposure items移除了大部分contamination signal，\n      G-MFRM的优势在于保留这些items的information（不丢弃）而非dramatically改变ranking。\n      vs sequential (p=0.018) 和 vs raw (p=0.001) 则显著，因为这些baseline完全不处理contamination。\n      Rank changes limited to 2个models移动≥2位，最大移动3位（Model-X-70B: raw rank 7→fair rank 10），\n      top-5有4/5不变——这限制了\"G-MFRM dramatically corrects rankings\"的narrative，\n      但支持\"G-MFRM provides correction where needed + diagnostic visibility everywhere\"的Tier B framing。\n      UDA的τ=0.84与sequential持平，说明neural K-factor adjustment在有contamination时也受confounding影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Main Results — Agreement with Chatbot Arena Human Votes\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"MT-Bench τ\", \"MT-Bench ρ\", \"Arena-Hard τ\", \"Arena-Hard ρ\", \"p vs G-MFRM\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Raw Multi-Judge Avg\", \"0.79\", \"0.83\", \"0.78\", \"0.82\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"MFRM-only\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.009\"]\n          - [\"Sequential Pipeline\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge + Discard\", \"0.85\", \"0.89\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.073\"]\n          - [\"DCR Factor\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.80\", \"0.84\", \"0.005\"]\n          - [\"UDA\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"Pref. Leakage Cal.\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.008\"]\n          - [\"**G-MFRM (ours)**\", \"**0.87**\", \"**0.91**\", \"**0.86**\", \"**0.90**\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 6: Rank Change Analysis (G-MFRM Fair vs Raw Average)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Raw Rank\", \"G-MFRM Rank\", \"Δ Rank\", \"c_n\", \"Moved ≥2?\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"1\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0.72\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", \"2\", \"3\", \"-1\", \"1.15\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"3\", \"2\", \"+1\", \"0.21\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", \"4\", \"5\", \"-1\", \"0.65\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Model-Y-Pro\", \"6\", \"4\", \"+2\", \"0.12\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Model-X-70B\", \"7\", \"10\", \"-3\", \"1.28\", \"Yes\"]\n      - name: \"Table 6b: Top-k Stability\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Overlap(raw, G-MFRM)\", \"Overlap(CJ+discard, G-MFRM)\", \"Overlap(sequential, G-MFRM)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"5\", \"4/5 (80%)\", \"5/5 (100%)\", \"4/5 (80%)\"]\n          - [\"10\", \"7/10 (70%)\", \"9/10 (90%)\", \"8/10 (80%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Bar chart of Kendall-τ across all methods, both benchmarks side by side. G-MFRM highest but margin small.\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Rank comparison alluvial diagram — raw ranks → G-MFRM fair ranks, highlighting the 2 models with ≥2 position change.\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Diagnostic output comparison matrix — checkmarks for which methods provide θ, d_j, c_n, e_i outputs. Only G-MFRM provides all four.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM在所有metrics上numerically best，但vs CyclicJudge+discard的优势borderline (p=0.073)。\n      这正是median档Tier B narrative的触发条件。\n      Fig 7（diagnostic output comparison）成为关键卖点：所有baseline只输出corrected scores，\n      G-MFRM额外输出per-model c_n、per-item e_i、per-judge d_j——这是unique contribution。\n      Rank change分析显示corrections targeted：Model-X-70B下降3位（c_n=1.28，最重contamination），\n      但大多数模型rank变化≤1位，说明moderate contamination下校正是surgical而非sweeping。\n\n  - name: contamination_magnitude_calibration\n    plan_id: exp-005\n    description: >\n      将exp-003的fitted c_n与MVP synthetic assumptions对比，确定real contamination magnitude所在区间。\n    expected_results:\n      c_n_median_fitted: 0.48\n      c_n_mean_fitted: 0.54\n      c_n_p25: 0.18\n      c_n_p75: 0.78\n      closest_mvp: \"between mvp_001 (c~0.5) and mvp_002 (c~1.5), closer to mvp_001\"\n      tier_determination: \"median → Tier B\"\n      models_with_c_n_gt_1: 2\n      models_with_c_n_lt_0_1: 5\n      c_n_distribution_shape: \"right-skewed, mode near 0.2, long tail to ~1.35\"\n      constat_delta_vs_c_n_spearman: 0.52\n      constat_delta_vs_c_n_pearson: 0.47\n    result_rationale: >\n      c_n median=0.48直接落在median档定义的[0.3, 0.8)区间内。这接近mvp_001（c~0.5）而非mvp_002/003（c~1.5）。\n      分布右偏（mode~0.2, median~0.48, mean~0.54）反映了真实情况：大多数模型contamination轻微，\n      少数模型（likely trained on leaked benchmark data）有较高contamination。\n      仅2个模型的c_n > 1.0，说明\"heavy contamination\"是exception而非norm——\n      这解释了为什么G-MFRM的ranking improvement modest：只有少数模型需要大幅校正。\n      ConStat validation ρ=0.52（[0.4, 0.7)范围）提供了moderate external validation，\n      说明c_n captures real contamination signal但不是perfect proxy（ConStat measures different aspect）。\n      这个结果正式触发Tier B narrative decision。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Contamination Magnitude — Real vs Synthetic\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Real Data (exp-003)\", \"MVP_001 (synthetic)\", \"MVP_002 (synthetic)\", \"MVP_003 (synthetic)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"c_n median\", \"0.48\", \"0.50\", \"1.50\", \"1.50\"]\n          - [\"c_n mean\", \"0.54\", \"0.50\", \"1.50\", \"1.50\"]\n          - [\"c_n std\", \"0.35\", \"0.10\", \"0.30\", \"0.30\"]\n          - [\"c_n range\", \"[0.05, 1.35]\", \"[0.3, 0.7]\", \"[0.8, 2.0]\", \"[0.8, 2.0]\"]\n          - [\"% models c_n > 0.8\", \"18%\", \"0%\", \"100%\", \"100%\"]\n      - name: \"Table S5: ConStat Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"95% CI\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Spearman ρ (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.52\", \"[0.31, 0.69]\"]\n          - [\"Pearson r (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.47\", \"[0.25, 0.65]\"]\n          - [\"Kendall τ (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.38\", \"[0.18, 0.55]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: c_n distribution overlay — real data (histogram) vs MVP_001 and MVP_003 synthetic (density curves). Real data closest to MVP_001 but with heavier tail.\"\n      - \"Fig 9: Scatter plot of ConStat per-model Δ vs G-MFRM c_n, with ρ=0.52 annotated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      This is the tier-determining experiment. c_n median=0.48确认Tier B。\n      关键implication：ranking correction虽然有效但不dramatic，paper必须pivot to diagnostic contribution。\n      但分布的heavy tail（2个模型c_n > 1.0）提供了\"contamination can be severe for specific models\"的evidence，\n      支持forward-looking argument：\"as contamination grows, joint estimation becomes increasingly critical。\"\n      ConStat中等验证(ρ=0.52)说明c_n不是noise但也不是perfect——足以claim validity，不足以claim definitive。\n\n  - name: judge_count_sensitivity\n    plan_id: exp-006\n    description: >\n      Judge数量敏感性分析：2/4/6/8个judges下G-MFRM performance degradation。\n    expected_results:\n      tau_2_judges: 0.81\n      tau_4_judges: 0.85\n      tau_6_judges: 0.86\n      tau_8_judges: 0.87\n      tau_2_judges_mfrm_only: 0.80\n      tau_4_judges_mfrm_only: 0.82\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_2_judges: 0.00\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_4_judges: 0.01\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_6_judges: 0.02\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_8_judges: 0.03\n      min_judges_for_significant_gain: 5\n      convergence_2_judges_max_rhat: 1.25\n      convergence_4_judges_max_rhat: 1.09\n      convergence_6_judges_max_rhat: 1.08\n      convergence_8_judges_max_rhat: 1.07\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设min judge count for significant gain在[4, 6]范围。预测5个judges是拐点。\n      2 judges时G-MFRM无法区分judge severity和contamination（under-identified），\n      退化到MFRM-level（τ=0.81 vs MFRM τ=0.80），R̂=1.25表明不收敛——\n      这是graceful degradation的empirical validation。\n      4 judges开始有信号但gain仍小（Δτ=+0.01），因为moderate contamination下\n      4个judge的cross-information不足以精确估计c_n posterior。\n      6-8 judges时gain stabilize（Δτ=+0.02-0.03），c_n posterior tighten。\n      这个结果支持\"≥5 judges recommended\"的practitioner guidance，\n      也诚实地展示了G-MFRM的practical limitation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Judge Count Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"# Judges\", \"G-MFRM τ\", \"Sequential τ\", \"Δτ\", \"Max R̂\", \"Min ESS\", \"Significant? (p<0.05)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"0.81\", \"0.81\", \"0.00\", \"1.25\", \"35\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"0.85\", \"0.84\", \"+0.01\", \"1.09\", \"92\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"0.86\", \"0.84\", \"+0.02\", \"1.08\", \"115\", \"Yes (p=0.04)\"]\n          - [\"6\", \"0.86\", \"0.84\", \"+0.02\", \"1.08\", \"128\", \"Yes (p=0.03)\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.87\", \"0.84\", \"+0.03\", \"1.07\", \"142\", \"Yes (p=0.02)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Line plot of Kendall-τ vs judge count for G-MFRM, MFRM, sequential, and raw average. G-MFRM curve diverges from sequential at 4+ judges.\"\n      - \"Fig S6: R̂ and ESS vs judge count, showing convergence improves monotonically.\"\n    analysis: >\n      实用建议：5个judges是cost-benefit sweet spot。2个judges时G-MFRM无害（graceful degradation to MFRM）\n      但也无contamination-correction benefit。\n      Addresses Reviewer Concern #8：cost-benefit明确，4 judges下G-MFRM不worse than MFRM，\n      practitioners不需要担心\"judges不够多时method会hurt\"。\n\n  - name: exposure_indicator_ablation\n    plan_id: exp-007\n    description: >\n      Leave-one-out ablation：每次移除一个e_i source，测量对downstream θ̂质量的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      # Full pipeline (3 sources)\n      full_tau: 0.87\n      full_c_n_recovery_rmse: 0.22\n      # Leave out LogProber\n      no_logprober_tau: 0.865\n      no_logprober_c_n_rmse: 0.24\n      no_logprober_delta_tau: -0.005\n      # Leave out Temporal\n      no_temporal_tau: 0.86\n      no_temporal_c_n_rmse: 0.26\n      no_temporal_delta_tau: -0.01\n      # Leave out Primary (performance gap)\n      no_primary_tau: 0.83\n      no_primary_c_n_rmse: 0.38\n      no_primary_delta_tau: -0.04\n      # Only Primary\n      only_primary_tau: 0.86\n      only_primary_c_n_rmse: 0.27\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设\"one source contributes little\"，这里是LogProber。\n      去除LogProber几乎不影响downstream performance（Δτ=-0.005），因为：\n      (1) LogProber覆盖率仅55%，缺失模型需要impute；\n      (2) LogProber与primary source的correlation最低（r=0.41），其unique information有限；\n      (3) moderate contamination下，token-level memorization信号弱于item-level performance gap。\n      去除temporal影响稍大（Δτ=-0.01）但仍modest，因覆盖率仅45%。\n      去除primary source影响显著（Δτ=-0.04），因它是唯一100%覆盖的source且与contamination最直接相关。\n      关键结论：2/3 sources (primary + temporal) 几乎match full pipeline，\n      这简化了practitioners的pipeline——不需要LogProber access也能获得good e_i estimates。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Exposure Indicator Ablation\"\n        columns: [\"Configuration\", \"Sources Used\", \"e_i Coverage\", \"G-MFRM τ\", \"c_n RMSE\", \"Δτ vs Full\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Full Pipeline\", \"Primary + Temporal + LogProber\", \"100%\", \"0.870\", \"0.22\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"−LogProber\", \"Primary + Temporal\", \"100%\", \"0.865\", \"0.24\", \"−0.005\"]\n          - [\"−Temporal\", \"Primary + LogProber\", \"100%\", \"0.860\", \"0.26\", \"−0.010\"]\n          - [\"−Primary\", \"Temporal + LogProber\", \"55%\", \"0.830\", \"0.38\", \"−0.040\"]\n          - [\"Primary Only\", \"Primary\", \"100%\", \"0.860\", \"0.27\", \"−0.010\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Bar chart of Kendall-τ for each ablation configuration, with error bars from bootstrap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Primary source是backbone，贡献最大。LogProber可被省略（对practitioners友好）。\n      Temporal有marginal但real contribution（+0.005 τ over primary-only），值得保留但non-essential。\n      这支持了\"2/3 sources sufficient\"的median档预期。\n      论文中应强调primary source的simplicity（仅需original + rephrased variants的performance gap），\n      降低method的perceived complexity。\n\n  - name: facet_fit_diagnostics\n    plan_id: exp-008\n    description: >\n      Measurement quality validation：infit/outfit MNSQ, person-fit (lz, EMRi),\n      divergent transitions, posterior predictive checks, trace plots。\n    expected_results:\n      # Infit/Outfit\n      theta_infit_mnsq_range: [0.72, 1.35]\n      theta_outfit_mnsq_range: [0.68, 1.42]\n      theta_misfitting_count: 2  # out of 22\n      item_infit_mnsq_range: [0.78, 1.28]\n      item_misfitting_count: 5  # out of 180\n      judge_infit_mnsq_range: [0.82, 1.22]\n      judge_misfitting_count: 1\n      c_n_infit_mnsq_range: [0.65, 1.48]\n      c_n_misfitting_count: 3\n      # Person-fit comparison\n      stage1_lz_flagged_models: 4\n      stage3_cn_gt_0_8_models: 4\n      overlap_lz_and_cn: 3  # 3 of 4 models flagged by both\n      # Posterior predictive\n      ppc_mean_residual: 0.02\n      ppc_95pct_residuals_in_band: 91.5\n      # Divergent transitions\n      divergent_transitions_total: 12\n      divergent_transitions_pct: 0.075  # 12 / (4000*4)\n      # Trace quality\n      trace_quality_theta: \"good\"\n      trace_quality_c_n: \"adequate with slow mixing for 2 models\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下model fit \"works but not perfectly\"。\n      θ的infit/outfit大部分在[0.7, 1.3]可接受范围，2个models misfitting（可能是能力profile异常的模型，\n      如specialized coding model在非coding items上表现与Rasch unidimensionality不符）。\n      c_n的fit较差（3个misfitting），因为rank-1 assumption (c_n·e_i) 对某些models是approximate：\n      部分models的contamination pattern可能不proportional to item exposure，\n      但MNSQ < 1.5说明misfit不severe enough to invalidate model。\n      Person-fit comparison（Stage 1 lz vs Stage 3 c_n）显示3/4 overlap——\n      Stage 1检测为\"anomalous\"的模型在Stage 3被identified as contaminated，\n      这提供了construct coherence validation（contamination IS the source of person misfit）。\n      PPC 91.5%的residuals in 95% band略低于ideal（95%），12个divergent transitions (0.075%)\n      在可接受范围但提示c_n posterior geometry有局部困难。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Facet Fit Summary (Infit/Outfit MNSQ)\"\n        columns: [\"Facet\", \"N\", \"Infit Range\", \"Outfit Range\", \"Misfitting (>1.3 or <0.7)\", \"% Misfitting\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"θ (model ability)\", \"22\", \"[0.72, 1.35]\", \"[0.68, 1.42]\", \"2\", \"9.1%\"]\n          - [\"b (item difficulty)\", \"180\", \"[0.78, 1.28]\", \"[0.75, 1.32]\", \"5\", \"2.8%\"]\n          - [\"d (judge severity)\", \"8\", \"[0.82, 1.22]\", \"[0.80, 1.25]\", \"1\", \"12.5%\"]\n          - [\"c (contamination)\", \"22\", \"[0.65, 1.48]\", \"[0.62, 1.55]\", \"3\", \"13.6%\"]\n      - name: \"Table S7: Person-Fit Cross-Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Stage 1 lz\", \"Stage 1 Flag?\", \"Stage 3 c_n\", \"Stage 3 c_n > 0.8?\"]\n        note: \"3 of 4 lz-flagged models also have c_n > 0.8, supporting construct coherence.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Infit/Outfit MNSQ Wright Map for all facets.\"\n      - \"Fig S8: Posterior predictive check — observed vs predicted score distributions.\"\n      - \"Fig S9: Trace plots for c_n of 4 highest-contamination models.\"\n      - \"Fig S10: Stage 1 person-fit (lz) vs Stage 3 c_n scatter plot.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Overall model fit acceptable for a novel psychometric model on real LLM evaluation data.\n      c_n facet的fit稍弱是预期内的——rank-1 assumption是simplification，\n      但misfit程度（MNSQ < 1.5）不足以reject model。\n      Person-fit cross-validation（3/4 overlap）是一个强validation signal，\n      可在paper中作为\"contamination构念效度\"的证据。\n      Limitations应讨论c_n misfitting models和rank-1 assumption的局限性。\n\n  - name: confounding_formal_observation\n    plan_id: exp-009\n    description: >\n      Formal bias analysis + Monte Carlo validation + synthetic c_n recovery。\n      Frame as Observation (standard OVB)。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formal derivation\n      bias_direction: \"sign(Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i)) determines bias direction\"\n      bias_magnitude_first_order: \"O(σ_d · σ_c · ρ_{d,c·e})\"\n      # Monte Carlo (1000 reps, varying ρ_{d,c·e})\n      mc_rho_0_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.155\n      mc_rho_0_theta_rmse_joint: 0.150\n      mc_rho_0_3_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.168\n      mc_rho_0_3_theta_rmse_joint: 0.148\n      mc_rho_0_6_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.198\n      mc_rho_0_6_theta_rmse_joint: 0.145\n      mc_rho_0_6_degradation_pct: 36.6\n      # c_n recovery (synthetic, known ground truth)\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_low: 0.12\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_moderate: 0.22\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_high: 0.18\n      c_n_95ci_coverage_overall: 0.88\n      c_n_95ci_coverage_c_gt_0_8: 0.82\n      c_n_mean_bias: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      Monte Carlo在ρ=0时两方法RMSE接近（无confounding → no advantage），\n      但ρ=0.6时sequential的RMSE升36.6%——低于mvp_003的43.8%因为此Monte Carlo\n      使用更realistic的moderate contamination parameters（c_n ~ mvp_001 level而非mvp_003）。\n      c_n recovery RMSE在moderate contamination regime为0.22，落在[0.15, 0.3]范围——\n      moderate contamination比strong contamination更难recover（信号弱），\n      但比very weak contamination更容易（有足够信号区分contaminated vs clean）。\n      95% CI coverage 88% < nominal 95%，说明posterior略under-covers，\n      主要因为staged estimation（e_i fixed）低估了total uncertainty——这是honest limitation。\n      c_n > 0.8的coverage更低（82%），因为high-c_n models的posterior更sensitive to e_i error。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Sequential vs Joint Estimation Under Confounding (Monte Carlo)\"\n        columns: [\"ρ(d,c·e)\", \"θ-RMSE Sequential\", \"θ-RMSE Joint\", \"Degradation %\", \"p-value\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"0.0\", \"0.155±0.024\", \"0.150±0.026\", \"3.3%\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"0.158±0.025\", \"0.149±0.025\", \"6.0%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.168±0.027\", \"0.148±0.024\", \"13.5%\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"0.6\", \"0.198±0.031\", \"0.145±0.023\", \"36.6%\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.9\", \"0.265±0.042\", \"0.142±0.022\", \"86.6%\", \"< 0.001\"]\n      - name: \"Table S1: Synthetic c_n Recovery\"\n        columns: [\"True c_n Range\", \"N Models\", \"Recovery RMSE\", \"Mean Bias\", \"95% CI Coverage\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.3)\", \"7\", \"0.12\", \"+0.02\", \"92%\"]\n          - [\"[0.3, 0.8)\", \"9\", \"0.22\", \"+0.03\", \"88%\"]\n          - [\"[0.8, 1.5]\", \"4\", \"0.18\", \"+0.05\", \"82%\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", \"20\", \"0.19\", \"+0.03\", \"88%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1 (Section 2): Toy example showing confounding mechanism. Left: sequential pipeline with bias arrows. Right: G-MFRM joint estimation.\"\n      - \"Fig S1: θ-RMSE vs ρ curves for sequential (rising) and joint (flat), clearly showing confounding sensitivity.\"\n      - \"Fig S2: c_n scatter (true vs recovered) with 45° reference line and 95% CI bands.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Observation成立：sequential estimator的bias随confounding strength单调增加，\n      joint estimator对confounding robust。Moderate contamination regime（median档）下，\n      sequential degradation ~13-37%（取决于ρ），G-MFRM consistently better。\n      c_n recovery RMSE=0.22支持\"G-MFRM can meaningfully estimate contamination\"但\n      coverage < 95%是honest limitation。\n      Paper Section 2应lead with这个Observation + toy example figure作为motivation。\n\n  - name: error_propagation_sensitivity\n    plan_id: exp-012\n    description: >\n      Staged estimation的error propagation：向e_i注入σ=0.1/0.2/0.5的Gaussian noise，\n      测量θ̂ RMSE degradation和c_n recovery accuracy。\n    expected_results:\n      # θ RMSE degradation\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_0: 0.145\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_1: 0.152\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_2: 0.168\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_5: 0.225\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_1_pct: 4.8\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_2_pct: 15.9\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_5_pct: 55.2\n      # c_n recovery\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_0: 0.19\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_1: 0.22\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_2: 0.30\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_5: 0.52\n      # Still beats sequential?\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_1: true\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_2: true\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_5: false\n      breakeven_sigma: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设σ=0.2时degradation在[5%, 15%]范围。预测15.9%接近上界，\n      因为moderate contamination下θ̂对e_i noise更sensitive——\n      当c_n本身较小时，e_i的noise相对于c_n·e_i signal的比例更大。\n      σ=0.1时degradation ~5%（可接受），σ=0.5时degradation ~55%（不可接受，method breaks down）。\n      Breakeven point σ≈0.38：e_i noise超过此阈值时G-MFRM不再优于sequential。\n      这是Tier B narrative的重要组成部分——staged estimation在reasonable e_i quality下robust，\n      但有clear failure mode。Paper Limitations必须讨论。\n      c_n recovery RMSE的degradation更steep（0.19→0.52 at σ=0.5），\n      因为c_n directly depends on e_i through gating mechanism。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Error Propagation Sensitivity (Synthetic)\"\n        columns: [\"e_i Noise σ\", \"θ̂ RMSE\", \"Degradation %\", \"c_n RMSE\", \"Beats Sequential?\", \"p vs Sequential\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"0.0 (oracle)\", \"0.145\", \"—\", \"0.19\", \"Yes\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"0.152\", \"4.8%\", \"0.22\", \"Yes\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.2\", \"0.168\", \"15.9%\", \"0.30\", \"Yes\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.192\", \"32.4%\", \"0.39\", \"Marginal\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"0.225\", \"55.2%\", \"0.52\", \"No\", \"0.35\"]\n      - name: \"Table S8: Breakeven Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Breakeven σ (G-MFRM τ = Sequential τ)\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"Estimated real e_i pipeline σ\", \"0.15–0.20\"]\n          - [\"Safety margin\", \"1.9–2.5×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: θ̂ RMSE vs e_i noise σ, with sequential baseline as horizontal dashed line. Intersection at σ≈0.38.\"\n      - \"Fig S11: c_n recovery scatter plots at each noise level, showing increasing dispersion.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Staged estimation在realistic noise levels下robust（safety margin ~2×），\n      但不是unconditionally robust。σ=0.2时degradation 15.9%处于acceptable-but-noticeable range。\n      Breakeven σ=0.38 vs estimated real pipeline σ=0.15-0.20 gives safety margin of ~2×。\n      This directly addresses Reviewer Concern #4b和Dream R1-N1：\n      staged estimation是principled且empirically robust，但paper必须state the limitation clearly。\n\n  - name: wildbench_replication\n    plan_id: exp-010\n    description: >\n      WildBench上复现G-MFRM pipeline作为第三个benchmark。Cross-benchmark generalization。\n    expected_results:\n      wildbench_num_items: 1024\n      wildbench_num_judges_used: 6  # subset due to cost\n      tau_raw_average: 0.76\n      tau_mfrm_only: 0.79\n      tau_sequential: 0.81\n      tau_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.82\n      tau_gmfrm: 0.84\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline: 0.02\n      c_n_median_wildbench: 0.38\n      c_n_correlation_with_mtbench: 0.72\n      convergence_max_rhat: 1.09\n      convergence_min_ess: 108\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_best_p: 0.065\n    result_rationale: >\n      WildBench的contamination预期更低（c_n median=0.38 vs MT-Bench 0.48），\n      因为WildBench items更diverse且更新更频繁。\n      6个judges（cost constraint）接近minimum threshold（exp-006预测5个为拐点），\n      所以convergence和performance都marginal worse than MT-Bench/Arena-Hard。\n      Δτ=+0.02 vs best baseline，p=0.065——again borderline，consistent with median档。\n      Cross-benchmark c_n correlation r=0.72说明contamination是model-level trait\n      （某些模型consistently contaminated across benchmarks），这是有价值的diagnostic insight。\n      WildBench主要价值是generalization evidence，即使improvement modest。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: WildBench Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Kendall-τ\", \"Spearman-ρ\", \"p vs G-MFRM\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Raw Average\", \"0.76\", \"0.80\", \"0.003\"]\n          - [\"Sequential\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.031\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge+Discard\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.065\"]\n          - [\"**G-MFRM**\", \"**0.84**\", \"**0.88**\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S12: Cross-benchmark c_n correlation scatter (MT-Bench c_n vs WildBench c_n), r=0.72.\"\n    analysis: >\n      WildBench replication确认G-MFRM在第三个benchmark上也numerically best，但advantage同样modest。\n      Cross-benchmark c_n correlation是strong secondary finding：\n      contamination susceptibility is a model property, not a benchmark artifact——\n      strengthens the case for per-model contamination audit as diagnostic tool。\n      Whether to include in main paper depends on page budget；可放appendix if space-constrained。\n\n  - name: adversarial_robustness\n    plan_id: exp-011\n    description: >\n      按Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) fragility findings测试G-MFRM robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      # Adversarial scenarios\n      scenario_judge_collusion_tau_drop: 0.04\n      scenario_strategic_contamination_tau_drop: 0.06\n      scenario_item_poisoning_tau_drop: 0.03\n      # Comparison: how much do baselines degrade?\n      baseline_sequential_collusion_tau_drop: 0.07\n      baseline_cyclicjudge_collusion_tau_drop: 0.05\n      # Detection\n      gmfrm_detects_collusion_via_d_j_outlier: true\n      gmfrm_detects_strategic_contam_via_c_n_pattern: \"partially\"\n      # Overall\n      gmfrm_more_robust_than_baselines: \"mixed — more robust to judge collusion, similarly vulnerable to strategic contamination\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下adversarial robustness预期为mixed results。\n      Judge collusion（部分judges协调inflate某模型）：G-MFRM的multi-facet estimation比sequential更robust\n      （Δτ drop 0.04 vs 0.07），因为d_j estimation可以部分absorb coordinated judge behavior。\n      Strategic contamination（模型deliberately leak but hide signals）：G-MFRM与baselines similarly vulnerable\n      （Δτ drop 0.06），因为e_i estimation依赖performance gap，deliberate obfuscation可以defeat this signal。\n      但G-MFRM的diagnostic outputs（d_j outlier detection）提供了detection capability其他方法没有。\n      这是P2 experiment——如果space允许放入paper，主要价值是demonstrates diagnostic use case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S10: Adversarial Robustness\"\n        columns: [\"Scenario\", \"G-MFRM τ Drop\", \"Sequential τ Drop\", \"CyclicJudge τ Drop\", \"G-MFRM Detects?\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Judge Collusion (2/8 judges)\", \"−0.04\", \"−0.07\", \"−0.05\", \"Yes (d_j outlier)\"]\n          - [\"Strategic Contamination\", \"−0.06\", \"−0.06\", \"−0.06\", \"Partial (c_n pattern)\"]\n          - [\"Item Poisoning (10% items)\", \"−0.03\", \"−0.04\", \"−0.03\", \"Yes (infit outlier)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S13: τ degradation under each adversarial scenario, comparing methods.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM不是adversarially robust的silver bullet，但diagnostic outputs提供了detection capability。\n      Judge collusion detection通过d_j outlier是实际可行的——这是\"judge selection guidance\"贡献的具体体现。\n      Paper中如果include，应framing为\"G-MFRM's diagnostic outputs enable detection of evaluation manipulation\"，\n      而非\"G-MFRM is robust to adversarial attack\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12445,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12445},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af9c2bc3-9f18-4e08-9e81-79982f6c114b","uuid":"35666280-0733-4d63-9cb8-c5f2bab44cbb"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":280883,"duration_api_ms":282442,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Tier B narrative. Real contamination is detectable but moderate (c_n median ~0.5).\n  G-MFRM ranking improvement over best baselines is statistically significant but practically modest (+2-3pp Kendall-τ).\n  Pivot primary contribution to diagnostic/interpretability outputs: per-model c_n as training data audit tool,\n  per-item e_i for item retirement decisions, per-judge d_j for judge selection guidance.\n  Lead argument: 'Sequential methods provide no visibility into whether corrections are needed —\n  G-MFRM provides both correction and diagnosis.' Forward-looking: as contamination grows, joint estimation becomes critical.\n  May need exp-010 (WildBench) to strengthen empirical package with a third benchmark.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: multi_judge_data_collection\n    plan_id: exp-001\n    description: >\n      Collect multi-judge evaluation data on MT-Bench and Arena-Hard using 8 judges.\n      20+ target models evaluated with position swap.\n    expected_results:\n      num_judges: 8\n      num_target_models: 22\n      benchmarks: [\"MT-Bench\", \"Arena-Hard\"]\n      total_judgments_mt_bench: 28160  # 22 models × 80 items × 8 judges × 2 positions\n      total_judgments_arena_hard: 35200  # 22 models × 100 items × 8 judges × 2 positions\n      position_bias_detected_judges: 3\n      api_cost_usd: 820\n      gpu_hours_used: 118\n      missing_data_pct: 2.1\n      inter_judge_agreement_fleiss_kappa: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下，8个judge的评分会展现出中等程度的一致性（Fleiss κ~0.38），反映了judge之间severity差异的真实存在。\n      22个target model覆盖了从GPT-5.5到开源7B模型的能力梯度，确保contamination susceptibility的变异性。\n      Position bias在3个judge上显著（主要是较小的开源judge），这为d_j估计提供了必要的judge间变异。\n      缺失数据约2%来自API超时和vLLM偶发OOM，在可接受范围内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Judge × Benchmark Data Collection Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"MT-Bench Items\", \"Arena-Hard Items\", \"Position Swap\", \"Missing %\", \"Mean Score\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.82\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.45\"]\n          - [\"Claude Sonnet 4.6\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"0.0%\", \"7.61\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"1.8%\", \"7.28\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"2.5%\", \"7.15\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3.6-27B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"4.2%\", \"6.93\"]\n          - [\"Llama 4 Maverick\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"3.1%\", \"7.05\"]\n          - [\"Gemma3-27B\", 1760, 2200, \"Yes\", \"2.8%\", \"6.88\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: Judge score distribution heatmap (judge × target model), showing systematic severity differences across judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      数据收集本身不直接验证claim，但数据质量决定了后续实验的上限。\n      Judge间score分布差异（mean range: 6.88–7.82）确认了judge severity变异的存在，为d_j估计提供信号。\n      中等的inter-judge agreement (κ~0.38) 意味着judge bias correction有实际意义。\n\n  - name: item_exposure_estimation\n    plan_id: exp-002\n    description: >\n      三源pipeline估计per-item exposure e_i。Primary source: 原始vs改写变体的performance gap；\n      Temporal: pre/post-cutoff变体gap；LogProber: token logprob memorization scores。\n      加权组合后用ConStat per-model delta做外部验证。\n    expected_results:\n      num_items_mt_bench: 80\n      num_items_arena_hard: 100\n      reference_variants_created: 180\n      primary_source_coverage: 1.0\n      temporal_source_coverage: 0.45\n      logprober_source_coverage: 0.55\n      composite_e_i_mean: 0.32\n      composite_e_i_std: 0.21\n      composite_e_i_range: [0.0, 0.82]\n      high_exposure_items_pct: 18.0  # e_i > 0.5\n      primary_temporal_correlation: 0.58\n      primary_logprober_correlation: 0.41\n      weighted_composite_internal_consistency_alpha: 0.62\n      constat_cn_vs_gmfrm_cn_spearman: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设real contamination moderate，因此e_i分布右偏但不极端：大部分items（~82%）的e_i < 0.5，\n      仅少数items（~18%）有明显的contamination exposure。这与\"contamination exists but is moderate\"一致。\n      Primary source（performance gap）覆盖率100%且信号最强；temporal source覆盖率有限（仅45%的items有\n      pre/post-cutoff变体），但与primary的相关性中等（r=0.58）。LogProber覆盖率55%（仅有logprob API的模型），\n      且与primary相关性较弱（r=0.41）——这是median档的关键特征之一：\"one source contributes little\"。\n      内部一致性α=0.62反映了三源信号的中等coherence，足以构建可用的composite但不overwhelming。\n      ConStat验证ρ=0.52落在[0.4, 0.7)范围内，表明fitted c_n与外部contamination measure有中等agreement。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Exposure Indicator Source Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Source\", \"Coverage\", \"Mean e_i\", \"Std\", \"Correlation w/ Composite\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Primary (performance gap)\", \"100%\", \"0.30\", \"0.22\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"Temporal (pre/post cutoff)\", \"45%\", \"0.35\", \"0.25\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"LogProber (logprob)\", \"55%\", \"0.28\", \"0.19\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"Weighted Composite\", \"100%\", \"0.32\", \"0.21\", \"1.00\"]\n      - name: \"Table S2: High-Exposure Items (e_i > 0.5)\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"Item ID\", \"e_i\", \"Primary\", \"Temporal\", \"LogProber\", \"Category\"]\n        note: \"~32 items total (18% of 180). Concentrated in coding and math categories.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2(a): e_i histogram across all items, showing right-skewed distribution with mode near 0.15 and tail to 0.82.\"\n      - \"Fig 2(b): Source-pair scatter plots (primary vs temporal, primary vs LogProber) with regression lines.\"\n      - \"Fig S2: Per-benchmark e_i distribution comparison (MT-Bench vs Arena-Hard).\"\n    analysis: >\n      e_i pipeline产生合理的exposure estimates，但LogProber贡献有限。这意味着在ablation（exp-007）中，\n      去除LogProber对composite质量影响较小，2/3 sources sufficient。\n      MT-Bench的coding/math items的e_i系统性高于reasoning/writing items，\n      与contamination通过training data leakage的机制一致。\n      Arena-Hard的e_i整体略低于MT-Bench，可能因Arena-Hard更新更频繁、泄露窗口更短。\n\n  - name: gmfrm_real_data_fit\n    plan_id: exp-003\n    description: >\n      在exp-001/002的real data上拟合G-MFRM三阶段pipeline。\n      Stage 1: MFRM估计(θ,b,d)。Stage 2: 固定exp-002的e_i。Stage 3: Joint gated model。\n      输出fair scores θ̂并与Chatbot Arena Elo对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # Convergence\n      stage1_max_rhat: 1.02\n      stage1_min_ess: 380\n      stage3_max_rhat: 1.07\n      stage3_min_ess: 142\n      stage3_divergent_transitions: 12\n      # Parameters\n      theta_range: [-1.8, 2.1]\n      d_j_range: [-0.62, 0.48]\n      d_j_std: 0.31\n      c_n_median: 0.48\n      c_n_mean: 0.54\n      c_n_range: [0.05, 1.35]\n      c_n_gt_0_3_count: 13  # out of 22 models\n      c_n_gt_0_8_count: 4\n      # Fit quality\n      kendall_tau_arena_mt_bench: 0.87\n      kendall_tau_arena_arena_hard: 0.86\n      spearman_rho_arena_mt_bench: 0.91\n      spearman_rho_arena_arena_hard: 0.90\n      # Graceful degradation check\n      arena_hard_subset_low_contamination_tau_gmfrm: 0.88\n      arena_hard_subset_low_contamination_tau_mfrm: 0.87\n      runtime_seconds: 8400\n      mcmc_warmup: 2000\n      mcmc_samples: 4000\n      mcmc_chains: 4\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心特征在此实验集中体现。c_n median=0.48落在[0.3, 0.8)区间，\n      接近mvp_001的weak contamination而非mvp_003的strong contamination。\n      22个模型中13个有c_n > 0.3（moderate），仅4个有c_n > 0.8（heavy），\n      说明contamination普遍存在但幅度有限。\n      Stage 3收敛需要调优：R̂=1.07（≤1.10但不ideal）、ESS=142（≥100但远低于mvp_003的224），\n      12个divergent transitions提示geometry有困难但未破坏inference。\n      这是因为moderate contamination意味着c_n的posterior更diffuse（数据对c_n的约束力较弱），\n      MCMC更难探索。Kendall-τ=0.87落在[0.84, 0.9]范围，比raw average显著提升但不dramatic。\n      低contamination子集上G-MFRM与MFRM几乎无差异（0.88 vs 0.87），确认graceful degradation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: G-MFRM Convergence Diagnostics\"\n        columns: [\"Parameter Group\", \"Max R̂\", \"Min ESS\", \"Mean ESS\", \"Divergent Transitions\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"θ (model ability)\", \"1.03\", \"285\", \"420\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"b (item difficulty)\", \"1.02\", \"310\", \"465\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"d (judge severity)\", \"1.02\", \"340\", \"490\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"c (contamination)\", \"1.07\", \"142\", \"215\", \"12\"]\n      - name: \"Table 4: Per-Model Parameter Estimates (sorted by θ̂)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"θ̂ (fair)\", \"θ_raw\", \"c_n\", \"c_n 95%CI\", \"Rank_fair\", \"Rank_raw\", \"Δ Rank\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"1.95\", \"2.08\", \"0.72\", \"[0.38, 1.12]\", \"1\", \"1\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"1.82\", \"1.85\", \"0.21\", \"[0.03, 0.52]\", \"2\", \"3\", \"+1\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", \"1.71\", \"1.92\", \"1.15\", \"[0.68, 1.35]\", \"3\", \"2\", \"-1\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", \"1.45\", \"1.58\", \"0.65\", \"[0.31, 1.02]\", \"5\", \"4\", \"-1\"]\n          - [\"Model-X-70B\", \"0.85\", \"1.10\", \"1.28\", \"[0.85, 1.35]\", \"10\", \"7\", \"-3\"]\n          - [\"Small-7B-Chat\", \"-1.52\", \"-1.48\", \"0.08\", \"[0.01, 0.28]\", \"22\", \"22\", \"0\"]\n      - name: \"Table S3: Per-Judge Severity Estimates\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"d_j\", \"d_j 95%CI\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"-0.15\", \"[-0.32, 0.02]\", \"Slightly lenient\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"0.08\", \"[-0.10, 0.25]\", \"Near neutral\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3.6-27B\", \"0.48\", \"[0.28, 0.68]\", \"Most severe\"]\n          - [\"Llama 4 Maverick\", \"-0.62\", \"[-0.85, -0.40]\", \"Most lenient\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Scatter plot of θ̂_fair vs Chatbot Arena Elo, colored by c_n magnitude. High-c_n models pulled downward relative to raw scores.\"\n      - \"Fig 4: c_n posterior density plots for all 22 models, ordered by posterior median. Shows moderate contamination landscape.\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Trace plots for c_n of 4 highest-contamination models, showing adequate mixing despite slower convergence.\"\n      - \"Fig S4: θ̂_raw vs θ̂_fair with identity line; deviations annotated with model names.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM成功拟合real data，收敛可接受但不完美（c_n的ESS偏低）。\n      c_n median=0.48确认了median档预期：contamination存在且可量化，但幅度moderate。\n      关键发现：4个模型（DeepSeek-V4-Pro, Qwen3-235B-A22B, Model-X-70B, 另一个）的c_n > 0.8，\n      这些模型的fair score显著低于raw score，产生了有意义的rank changes。\n      但top-5整体稳定（仅1-2个位置变动），限制了ranking correction的headline impact。\n      Per-judge d_j range（-0.62 to 0.48）确认judge severity差异显著，\n      为\"judge selection guidance\"这一diagnostic贡献提供了直接证据。\n\n  - name: baseline_comparison\n    plan_id: exp-004\n    description: >\n      G-MFRM vs 8条baselines在相同数据上对比。\n      包含rank change analysis：具体哪些模型换位、换多少位、top-k稳定性。\n    expected_results:\n      # Kendall-τ with Chatbot Arena (MT-Bench)\n      tau_raw_average: 0.79\n      tau_mfrm_only: 0.82\n      tau_sequential: 0.84\n      tau_cyclicjudge: 0.83\n      tau_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.85\n      tau_dcr_factor: 0.81\n      tau_uda: 0.84\n      tau_pref_leakage_cal: 0.82\n      tau_gmfrm: 0.87\n      # Spearman-ρ with Chatbot Arena (MT-Bench)\n      rho_raw_average: 0.83\n      rho_mfrm_only: 0.86\n      rho_sequential: 0.88\n      rho_cyclicjudge: 0.87\n      rho_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.89\n      rho_dcr_factor: 0.85\n      rho_uda: 0.88\n      rho_pref_leakage_cal: 0.86\n      rho_gmfrm: 0.91\n      # Arena-Hard results similar pattern\n      tau_gmfrm_arena_hard: 0.86\n      tau_best_baseline_arena_hard: 0.84\n      # Δτ vs best baseline\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_mt_bench: 0.02\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline_arena_hard: 0.02\n      # Statistical significance\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_cyclicjudge_discard_p: 0.073\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_sequential_p: 0.018\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_raw_p: 0.001\n      # Rank change analysis\n      rank_changes_ge2_positions: 2\n      top5_stability_raw_vs_gmfrm: \"4/5 same\"\n      top10_stability_raw_vs_gmfrm: \"7/10 same\"\n      max_rank_change_model: \"Model-X-70B\"\n      max_rank_change_positions: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档的核心tension在此实验体现：G-MFRM beats all baselines但margin modest。\n      Δτ=+0.02 vs CyclicJudge+discard（best baseline），p=0.073——borderline significant。\n      这是因为moderate contamination意味着contamination correction的marginal value有限：\n      CyclicJudge+discard已经通过丢弃high-exposure items移除了大部分contamination signal，\n      G-MFRM的优势在于保留这些items的information（不丢弃）而非dramatically改变ranking。\n      vs sequential (p=0.018) 和 vs raw (p=0.001) 则显著，因为这些baseline完全不处理contamination。\n      Rank changes limited to 2个models移动≥2位，最大移动3位（Model-X-70B: raw rank 7→fair rank 10），\n      top-5有4/5不变——这限制了\"G-MFRM dramatically corrects rankings\"的narrative，\n      但支持\"G-MFRM provides correction where needed + diagnostic visibility everywhere\"的Tier B framing。\n      UDA的τ=0.84与sequential持平，说明neural K-factor adjustment在有contamination时也受confounding影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Main Results — Agreement with Chatbot Arena Human Votes\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"MT-Bench τ\", \"MT-Bench ρ\", \"Arena-Hard τ\", \"Arena-Hard ρ\", \"p vs G-MFRM\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Raw Multi-Judge Avg\", \"0.79\", \"0.83\", \"0.78\", \"0.82\", \"0.001\"]\n          - [\"MFRM-only\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.009\"]\n          - [\"Sequential Pipeline\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.018\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.025\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge + Discard\", \"0.85\", \"0.89\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.073\"]\n          - [\"DCR Factor\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.80\", \"0.84\", \"0.005\"]\n          - [\"UDA\", \"0.84\", \"0.88\", \"0.83\", \"0.87\", \"0.021\"]\n          - [\"Pref. Leakage Cal.\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.008\"]\n          - [\"**G-MFRM (ours)**\", \"**0.87**\", \"**0.91**\", \"**0.86**\", \"**0.90**\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 6: Rank Change Analysis (G-MFRM Fair vs Raw Average)\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Raw Rank\", \"G-MFRM Rank\", \"Δ Rank\", \"c_n\", \"Moved ≥2?\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"GPT-5.5\", \"1\", \"1\", \"0\", \"0.72\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"DeepSeek-V4-Pro\", \"2\", \"3\", \"-1\", \"1.15\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Claude Opus 4.7\", \"3\", \"2\", \"+1\", \"0.21\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-235B-A22B\", \"4\", \"5\", \"-1\", \"0.65\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"Model-Y-Pro\", \"6\", \"4\", \"+2\", \"0.12\", \"Yes\"]\n          - [\"Model-X-70B\", \"7\", \"10\", \"-3\", \"1.28\", \"Yes\"]\n      - name: \"Table 6b: Top-k Stability\"\n        columns: [\"k\", \"Overlap(raw, G-MFRM)\", \"Overlap(CJ+discard, G-MFRM)\", \"Overlap(sequential, G-MFRM)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"5\", \"4/5 (80%)\", \"5/5 (100%)\", \"4/5 (80%)\"]\n          - [\"10\", \"7/10 (70%)\", \"9/10 (90%)\", \"8/10 (80%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Bar chart of Kendall-τ across all methods, both benchmarks side by side. G-MFRM highest but margin small.\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Rank comparison alluvial diagram — raw ranks → G-MFRM fair ranks, highlighting the 2 models with ≥2 position change.\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Diagnostic output comparison matrix — checkmarks for which methods provide θ, d_j, c_n, e_i outputs. Only G-MFRM provides all four.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM在所有metrics上numerically best，但vs CyclicJudge+discard的优势borderline (p=0.073)。\n      这正是median档Tier B narrative的触发条件。\n      Fig 7（diagnostic output comparison）成为关键卖点：所有baseline只输出corrected scores，\n      G-MFRM额外输出per-model c_n、per-item e_i、per-judge d_j——这是unique contribution。\n      Rank change分析显示corrections targeted：Model-X-70B下降3位（c_n=1.28，最重contamination），\n      但大多数模型rank变化≤1位，说明moderate contamination下校正是surgical而非sweeping。\n\n  - name: contamination_magnitude_calibration\n    plan_id: exp-005\n    description: >\n      将exp-003的fitted c_n与MVP synthetic assumptions对比，确定real contamination magnitude所在区间。\n    expected_results:\n      c_n_median_fitted: 0.48\n      c_n_mean_fitted: 0.54\n      c_n_p25: 0.18\n      c_n_p75: 0.78\n      closest_mvp: \"between mvp_001 (c~0.5) and mvp_002 (c~1.5), closer to mvp_001\"\n      tier_determination: \"median → Tier B\"\n      models_with_c_n_gt_1: 2\n      models_with_c_n_lt_0_1: 5\n      c_n_distribution_shape: \"right-skewed, mode near 0.2, long tail to ~1.35\"\n      constat_delta_vs_c_n_spearman: 0.52\n      constat_delta_vs_c_n_pearson: 0.47\n    result_rationale: >\n      c_n median=0.48直接落在median档定义的[0.3, 0.8)区间内。这接近mvp_001（c~0.5）而非mvp_002/003（c~1.5）。\n      分布右偏（mode~0.2, median~0.48, mean~0.54）反映了真实情况：大多数模型contamination轻微，\n      少数模型（likely trained on leaked benchmark data）有较高contamination。\n      仅2个模型的c_n > 1.0，说明\"heavy contamination\"是exception而非norm——\n      这解释了为什么G-MFRM的ranking improvement modest：只有少数模型需要大幅校正。\n      ConStat validation ρ=0.52（[0.4, 0.7)范围）提供了moderate external validation，\n      说明c_n captures real contamination signal但不是perfect proxy（ConStat measures different aspect）。\n      这个结果正式触发Tier B narrative decision。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Contamination Magnitude — Real vs Synthetic\"\n        columns: [\"Statistic\", \"Real Data (exp-003)\", \"MVP_001 (synthetic)\", \"MVP_002 (synthetic)\", \"MVP_003 (synthetic)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"c_n median\", \"0.48\", \"0.50\", \"1.50\", \"1.50\"]\n          - [\"c_n mean\", \"0.54\", \"0.50\", \"1.50\", \"1.50\"]\n          - [\"c_n std\", \"0.35\", \"0.10\", \"0.30\", \"0.30\"]\n          - [\"c_n range\", \"[0.05, 1.35]\", \"[0.3, 0.7]\", \"[0.8, 2.0]\", \"[0.8, 2.0]\"]\n          - [\"% models c_n > 0.8\", \"18%\", \"0%\", \"100%\", \"100%\"]\n      - name: \"Table S5: ConStat Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"95% CI\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Spearman ρ (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.52\", \"[0.31, 0.69]\"]\n          - [\"Pearson r (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.47\", \"[0.25, 0.65]\"]\n          - [\"Kendall τ (ConStat Δ vs c_n)\", \"0.38\", \"[0.18, 0.55]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: c_n distribution overlay — real data (histogram) vs MVP_001 and MVP_003 synthetic (density curves). Real data closest to MVP_001 but with heavier tail.\"\n      - \"Fig 9: Scatter plot of ConStat per-model Δ vs G-MFRM c_n, with ρ=0.52 annotated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      This is the tier-determining experiment. c_n median=0.48确认Tier B。\n      关键implication：ranking correction虽然有效但不dramatic，paper必须pivot to diagnostic contribution。\n      但分布的heavy tail（2个模型c_n > 1.0）提供了\"contamination can be severe for specific models\"的evidence，\n      支持forward-looking argument：\"as contamination grows, joint estimation becomes increasingly critical。\"\n      ConStat中等验证(ρ=0.52)说明c_n不是noise但也不是perfect——足以claim validity，不足以claim definitive。\n\n  - name: judge_count_sensitivity\n    plan_id: exp-006\n    description: >\n      Judge数量敏感性分析：2/4/6/8个judges下G-MFRM performance degradation。\n    expected_results:\n      tau_2_judges: 0.81\n      tau_4_judges: 0.85\n      tau_6_judges: 0.86\n      tau_8_judges: 0.87\n      tau_2_judges_mfrm_only: 0.80\n      tau_4_judges_mfrm_only: 0.82\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_2_judges: 0.00\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_4_judges: 0.01\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_6_judges: 0.02\n      delta_gmfrm_vs_sequential_8_judges: 0.03\n      min_judges_for_significant_gain: 5\n      convergence_2_judges_max_rhat: 1.25\n      convergence_4_judges_max_rhat: 1.09\n      convergence_6_judges_max_rhat: 1.08\n      convergence_8_judges_max_rhat: 1.07\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设min judge count for significant gain在[4, 6]范围。预测5个judges是拐点。\n      2 judges时G-MFRM无法区分judge severity和contamination（under-identified），\n      退化到MFRM-level（τ=0.81 vs MFRM τ=0.80），R̂=1.25表明不收敛——\n      这是graceful degradation的empirical validation。\n      4 judges开始有信号但gain仍小（Δτ=+0.01），因为moderate contamination下\n      4个judge的cross-information不足以精确估计c_n posterior。\n      6-8 judges时gain stabilize（Δτ=+0.02-0.03），c_n posterior tighten。\n      这个结果支持\"≥5 judges recommended\"的practitioner guidance，\n      也诚实地展示了G-MFRM的practical limitation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Judge Count Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"# Judges\", \"G-MFRM τ\", \"Sequential τ\", \"Δτ\", \"Max R̂\", \"Min ESS\", \"Significant? (p<0.05)\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"2\", \"0.81\", \"0.81\", \"0.00\", \"1.25\", \"35\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"4\", \"0.85\", \"0.84\", \"+0.01\", \"1.09\", \"92\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"5\", \"0.86\", \"0.84\", \"+0.02\", \"1.08\", \"115\", \"Yes (p=0.04)\"]\n          - [\"6\", \"0.86\", \"0.84\", \"+0.02\", \"1.08\", \"128\", \"Yes (p=0.03)\"]\n          - [\"8\", \"0.87\", \"0.84\", \"+0.03\", \"1.07\", \"142\", \"Yes (p=0.02)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Line plot of Kendall-τ vs judge count for G-MFRM, MFRM, sequential, and raw average. G-MFRM curve diverges from sequential at 4+ judges.\"\n      - \"Fig S6: R̂ and ESS vs judge count, showing convergence improves monotonically.\"\n    analysis: >\n      实用建议：5个judges是cost-benefit sweet spot。2个judges时G-MFRM无害（graceful degradation to MFRM）\n      但也无contamination-correction benefit。\n      Addresses Reviewer Concern #8：cost-benefit明确，4 judges下G-MFRM不worse than MFRM，\n      practitioners不需要担心\"judges不够多时method会hurt\"。\n\n  - name: exposure_indicator_ablation\n    plan_id: exp-007\n    description: >\n      Leave-one-out ablation：每次移除一个e_i source，测量对downstream θ̂质量的影响。\n    expected_results:\n      # Full pipeline (3 sources)\n      full_tau: 0.87\n      full_c_n_recovery_rmse: 0.22\n      # Leave out LogProber\n      no_logprober_tau: 0.865\n      no_logprober_c_n_rmse: 0.24\n      no_logprober_delta_tau: -0.005\n      # Leave out Temporal\n      no_temporal_tau: 0.86\n      no_temporal_c_n_rmse: 0.26\n      no_temporal_delta_tau: -0.01\n      # Leave out Primary (performance gap)\n      no_primary_tau: 0.83\n      no_primary_c_n_rmse: 0.38\n      no_primary_delta_tau: -0.04\n      # Only Primary\n      only_primary_tau: 0.86\n      only_primary_c_n_rmse: 0.27\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设\"one source contributes little\"，这里是LogProber。\n      去除LogProber几乎不影响downstream performance（Δτ=-0.005），因为：\n      (1) LogProber覆盖率仅55%，缺失模型需要impute；\n      (2) LogProber与primary source的correlation最低（r=0.41），其unique information有限；\n      (3) moderate contamination下，token-level memorization信号弱于item-level performance gap。\n      去除temporal影响稍大（Δτ=-0.01）但仍modest，因覆盖率仅45%。\n      去除primary source影响显著（Δτ=-0.04），因它是唯一100%覆盖的source且与contamination最直接相关。\n      关键结论：2/3 sources (primary + temporal) 几乎match full pipeline，\n      这简化了practitioners的pipeline——不需要LogProber access也能获得good e_i estimates。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Exposure Indicator Ablation\"\n        columns: [\"Configuration\", \"Sources Used\", \"e_i Coverage\", \"G-MFRM τ\", \"c_n RMSE\", \"Δτ vs Full\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Full Pipeline\", \"Primary + Temporal + LogProber\", \"100%\", \"0.870\", \"0.22\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"−LogProber\", \"Primary + Temporal\", \"100%\", \"0.865\", \"0.24\", \"−0.005\"]\n          - [\"−Temporal\", \"Primary + LogProber\", \"100%\", \"0.860\", \"0.26\", \"−0.010\"]\n          - [\"−Primary\", \"Temporal + LogProber\", \"55%\", \"0.830\", \"0.38\", \"−0.040\"]\n          - [\"Primary Only\", \"Primary\", \"100%\", \"0.860\", \"0.27\", \"−0.010\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11: Bar chart of Kendall-τ for each ablation configuration, with error bars from bootstrap.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Primary source是backbone，贡献最大。LogProber可被省略（对practitioners友好）。\n      Temporal有marginal但real contribution（+0.005 τ over primary-only），值得保留但non-essential。\n      这支持了\"2/3 sources sufficient\"的median档预期。\n      论文中应强调primary source的simplicity（仅需original + rephrased variants的performance gap），\n      降低method的perceived complexity。\n\n  - name: facet_fit_diagnostics\n    plan_id: exp-008\n    description: >\n      Measurement quality validation：infit/outfit MNSQ, person-fit (lz, EMRi),\n      divergent transitions, posterior predictive checks, trace plots。\n    expected_results:\n      # Infit/Outfit\n      theta_infit_mnsq_range: [0.72, 1.35]\n      theta_outfit_mnsq_range: [0.68, 1.42]\n      theta_misfitting_count: 2  # out of 22\n      item_infit_mnsq_range: [0.78, 1.28]\n      item_misfitting_count: 5  # out of 180\n      judge_infit_mnsq_range: [0.82, 1.22]\n      judge_misfitting_count: 1\n      c_n_infit_mnsq_range: [0.65, 1.48]\n      c_n_misfitting_count: 3\n      # Person-fit comparison\n      stage1_lz_flagged_models: 4\n      stage3_cn_gt_0_8_models: 4\n      overlap_lz_and_cn: 3  # 3 of 4 models flagged by both\n      # Posterior predictive\n      ppc_mean_residual: 0.02\n      ppc_95pct_residuals_in_band: 91.5\n      # Divergent transitions\n      divergent_transitions_total: 12\n      divergent_transitions_pct: 0.075  # 12 / (4000*4)\n      # Trace quality\n      trace_quality_theta: \"good\"\n      trace_quality_c_n: \"adequate with slow mixing for 2 models\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下model fit \"works but not perfectly\"。\n      θ的infit/outfit大部分在[0.7, 1.3]可接受范围，2个models misfitting（可能是能力profile异常的模型，\n      如specialized coding model在非coding items上表现与Rasch unidimensionality不符）。\n      c_n的fit较差（3个misfitting），因为rank-1 assumption (c_n·e_i) 对某些models是approximate：\n      部分models的contamination pattern可能不proportional to item exposure，\n      但MNSQ < 1.5说明misfit不severe enough to invalidate model。\n      Person-fit comparison（Stage 1 lz vs Stage 3 c_n）显示3/4 overlap——\n      Stage 1检测为\"anomalous\"的模型在Stage 3被identified as contaminated，\n      这提供了construct coherence validation（contamination IS the source of person misfit）。\n      PPC 91.5%的residuals in 95% band略低于ideal（95%），12个divergent transitions (0.075%)\n      在可接受范围但提示c_n posterior geometry有局部困难。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Facet Fit Summary (Infit/Outfit MNSQ)\"\n        columns: [\"Facet\", \"N\", \"Infit Range\", \"Outfit Range\", \"Misfitting (>1.3 or <0.7)\", \"% Misfitting\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"θ (model ability)\", \"22\", \"[0.72, 1.35]\", \"[0.68, 1.42]\", \"2\", \"9.1%\"]\n          - [\"b (item difficulty)\", \"180\", \"[0.78, 1.28]\", \"[0.75, 1.32]\", \"5\", \"2.8%\"]\n          - [\"d (judge severity)\", \"8\", \"[0.82, 1.22]\", \"[0.80, 1.25]\", \"1\", \"12.5%\"]\n          - [\"c (contamination)\", \"22\", \"[0.65, 1.48]\", \"[0.62, 1.55]\", \"3\", \"13.6%\"]\n      - name: \"Table S7: Person-Fit Cross-Validation\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"Stage 1 lz\", \"Stage 1 Flag?\", \"Stage 3 c_n\", \"Stage 3 c_n > 0.8?\"]\n        note: \"3 of 4 lz-flagged models also have c_n > 0.8, supporting construct coherence.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Infit/Outfit MNSQ Wright Map for all facets.\"\n      - \"Fig S8: Posterior predictive check — observed vs predicted score distributions.\"\n      - \"Fig S9: Trace plots for c_n of 4 highest-contamination models.\"\n      - \"Fig S10: Stage 1 person-fit (lz) vs Stage 3 c_n scatter plot.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Overall model fit acceptable for a novel psychometric model on real LLM evaluation data.\n      c_n facet的fit稍弱是预期内的——rank-1 assumption是simplification，\n      但misfit程度（MNSQ < 1.5）不足以reject model。\n      Person-fit cross-validation（3/4 overlap）是一个强validation signal，\n      可在paper中作为\"contamination构念效度\"的证据。\n      Limitations应讨论c_n misfitting models和rank-1 assumption的局限性。\n\n  - name: confounding_formal_observation\n    plan_id: exp-009\n    description: >\n      Formal bias analysis + Monte Carlo validation + synthetic c_n recovery。\n      Frame as Observation (standard OVB)。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formal derivation\n      bias_direction: \"sign(Cov(d_j, c_n·e_i)) determines bias direction\"\n      bias_magnitude_first_order: \"O(σ_d · σ_c · ρ_{d,c·e})\"\n      # Monte Carlo (1000 reps, varying ρ_{d,c·e})\n      mc_rho_0_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.155\n      mc_rho_0_theta_rmse_joint: 0.150\n      mc_rho_0_3_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.168\n      mc_rho_0_3_theta_rmse_joint: 0.148\n      mc_rho_0_6_theta_rmse_sequential: 0.198\n      mc_rho_0_6_theta_rmse_joint: 0.145\n      mc_rho_0_6_degradation_pct: 36.6\n      # c_n recovery (synthetic, known ground truth)\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_low: 0.12\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_moderate: 0.22\n      c_n_recovery_rmse_c_high: 0.18\n      c_n_95ci_coverage_overall: 0.88\n      c_n_95ci_coverage_c_gt_0_8: 0.82\n      c_n_mean_bias: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      Monte Carlo在ρ=0时两方法RMSE接近（无confounding → no advantage），\n      但ρ=0.6时sequential的RMSE升36.6%——低于mvp_003的43.8%因为此Monte Carlo\n      使用更realistic的moderate contamination parameters（c_n ~ mvp_001 level而非mvp_003）。\n      c_n recovery RMSE在moderate contamination regime为0.22，落在[0.15, 0.3]范围——\n      moderate contamination比strong contamination更难recover（信号弱），\n      但比very weak contamination更容易（有足够信号区分contaminated vs clean）。\n      95% CI coverage 88% < nominal 95%，说明posterior略under-covers，\n      主要因为staged estimation（e_i fixed）低估了total uncertainty——这是honest limitation。\n      c_n > 0.8的coverage更低（82%），因为high-c_n models的posterior更sensitive to e_i error。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Sequential vs Joint Estimation Under Confounding (Monte Carlo)\"\n        columns: [\"ρ(d,c·e)\", \"θ-RMSE Sequential\", \"θ-RMSE Joint\", \"Degradation %\", \"p-value\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"0.0\", \"0.155±0.024\", \"0.150±0.026\", \"3.3%\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"0.158±0.025\", \"0.149±0.025\", \"6.0%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.168±0.027\", \"0.148±0.024\", \"13.5%\", \"0.04\"]\n          - [\"0.6\", \"0.198±0.031\", \"0.145±0.023\", \"36.6%\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.9\", \"0.265±0.042\", \"0.142±0.022\", \"86.6%\", \"< 0.001\"]\n      - name: \"Table S1: Synthetic c_n Recovery\"\n        columns: [\"True c_n Range\", \"N Models\", \"Recovery RMSE\", \"Mean Bias\", \"95% CI Coverage\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"[0, 0.3)\", \"7\", \"0.12\", \"+0.02\", \"92%\"]\n          - [\"[0.3, 0.8)\", \"9\", \"0.22\", \"+0.03\", \"88%\"]\n          - [\"[0.8, 1.5]\", \"4\", \"0.18\", \"+0.05\", \"82%\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", \"20\", \"0.19\", \"+0.03\", \"88%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1 (Section 2): Toy example showing confounding mechanism. Left: sequential pipeline with bias arrows. Right: G-MFRM joint estimation.\"\n      - \"Fig S1: θ-RMSE vs ρ curves for sequential (rising) and joint (flat), clearly showing confounding sensitivity.\"\n      - \"Fig S2: c_n scatter (true vs recovered) with 45° reference line and 95% CI bands.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Observation成立：sequential estimator的bias随confounding strength单调增加，\n      joint estimator对confounding robust。Moderate contamination regime（median档）下，\n      sequential degradation ~13-37%（取决于ρ），G-MFRM consistently better。\n      c_n recovery RMSE=0.22支持\"G-MFRM can meaningfully estimate contamination\"但\n      coverage < 95%是honest limitation。\n      Paper Section 2应lead with这个Observation + toy example figure作为motivation。\n\n  - name: error_propagation_sensitivity\n    plan_id: exp-012\n    description: >\n      Staged estimation的error propagation：向e_i注入σ=0.1/0.2/0.5的Gaussian noise，\n      测量θ̂ RMSE degradation和c_n recovery accuracy。\n    expected_results:\n      # θ RMSE degradation\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_0: 0.145\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_1: 0.152\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_2: 0.168\n      theta_rmse_sigma_0_5: 0.225\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_1_pct: 4.8\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_2_pct: 15.9\n      theta_rmse_degradation_sigma_0_5_pct: 55.2\n      # c_n recovery\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_0: 0.19\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_1: 0.22\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_2: 0.30\n      c_n_rmse_sigma_0_5: 0.52\n      # Still beats sequential?\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_1: true\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_2: true\n      still_beats_sequential_sigma_0_5: false\n      breakeven_sigma: 0.38\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档假设σ=0.2时degradation在[5%, 15%]范围。预测15.9%接近上界，\n      因为moderate contamination下θ̂对e_i noise更sensitive——\n      当c_n本身较小时，e_i的noise相对于c_n·e_i signal的比例更大。\n      σ=0.1时degradation ~5%（可接受），σ=0.5时degradation ~55%（不可接受，method breaks down）。\n      Breakeven point σ≈0.38：e_i noise超过此阈值时G-MFRM不再优于sequential。\n      这是Tier B narrative的重要组成部分——staged estimation在reasonable e_i quality下robust，\n      但有clear failure mode。Paper Limitations必须讨论。\n      c_n recovery RMSE的degradation更steep（0.19→0.52 at σ=0.5），\n      因为c_n directly depends on e_i through gating mechanism。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Error Propagation Sensitivity (Synthetic)\"\n        columns: [\"e_i Noise σ\", \"θ̂ RMSE\", \"Degradation %\", \"c_n RMSE\", \"Beats Sequential?\", \"p vs Sequential\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"0.0 (oracle)\", \"0.145\", \"—\", \"0.19\", \"Yes\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.1\", \"0.152\", \"4.8%\", \"0.22\", \"Yes\", \"< 0.001\"]\n          - [\"0.2\", \"0.168\", \"15.9%\", \"0.30\", \"Yes\", \"0.02\"]\n          - [\"0.3\", \"0.192\", \"32.4%\", \"0.39\", \"Marginal\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"0.5\", \"0.225\", \"55.2%\", \"0.52\", \"No\", \"0.35\"]\n      - name: \"Table S8: Breakeven Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Breakeven σ (G-MFRM τ = Sequential τ)\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"Estimated real e_i pipeline σ\", \"0.15–0.20\"]\n          - [\"Safety margin\", \"1.9–2.5×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: θ̂ RMSE vs e_i noise σ, with sequential baseline as horizontal dashed line. Intersection at σ≈0.38.\"\n      - \"Fig S11: c_n recovery scatter plots at each noise level, showing increasing dispersion.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Staged estimation在realistic noise levels下robust（safety margin ~2×），\n      但不是unconditionally robust。σ=0.2时degradation 15.9%处于acceptable-but-noticeable range。\n      Breakeven σ=0.38 vs estimated real pipeline σ=0.15-0.20 gives safety margin of ~2×。\n      This directly addresses Reviewer Concern #4b和Dream R1-N1：\n      staged estimation是principled且empirically robust，但paper必须state the limitation clearly。\n\n  - name: wildbench_replication\n    plan_id: exp-010\n    description: >\n      WildBench上复现G-MFRM pipeline作为第三个benchmark。Cross-benchmark generalization。\n    expected_results:\n      wildbench_num_items: 1024\n      wildbench_num_judges_used: 6  # subset due to cost\n      tau_raw_average: 0.76\n      tau_mfrm_only: 0.79\n      tau_sequential: 0.81\n      tau_cyclicjudge_discard: 0.82\n      tau_gmfrm: 0.84\n      delta_tau_vs_best_baseline: 0.02\n      c_n_median_wildbench: 0.38\n      c_n_correlation_with_mtbench: 0.72\n      convergence_max_rhat: 1.09\n      convergence_min_ess: 108\n      wilcoxon_gmfrm_vs_best_p: 0.065\n    result_rationale: >\n      WildBench的contamination预期更低（c_n median=0.38 vs MT-Bench 0.48），\n      因为WildBench items更diverse且更新更频繁。\n      6个judges（cost constraint）接近minimum threshold（exp-006预测5个为拐点），\n      所以convergence和performance都marginal worse than MT-Bench/Arena-Hard。\n      Δτ=+0.02 vs best baseline，p=0.065——again borderline，consistent with median档。\n      Cross-benchmark c_n correlation r=0.72说明contamination是model-level trait\n      （某些模型consistently contaminated across benchmarks），这是有价值的diagnostic insight。\n      WildBench主要价值是generalization evidence，即使improvement modest。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: WildBench Results\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"Kendall-τ\", \"Spearman-ρ\", \"p vs G-MFRM\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Raw Average\", \"0.76\", \"0.80\", \"0.003\"]\n          - [\"Sequential\", \"0.81\", \"0.85\", \"0.031\"]\n          - [\"CyclicJudge+Discard\", \"0.82\", \"0.86\", \"0.065\"]\n          - [\"**G-MFRM**\", \"**0.84**\", \"**0.88**\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S12: Cross-benchmark c_n correlation scatter (MT-Bench c_n vs WildBench c_n), r=0.72.\"\n    analysis: >\n      WildBench replication确认G-MFRM在第三个benchmark上也numerically best，但advantage同样modest。\n      Cross-benchmark c_n correlation是strong secondary finding：\n      contamination susceptibility is a model property, not a benchmark artifact——\n      strengthens the case for per-model contamination audit as diagnostic tool。\n      Whether to include in main paper depends on page budget；可放appendix if space-constrained。\n\n  - name: adversarial_robustness\n    plan_id: exp-011\n    description: >\n      按Wang et al. (ICLR 2026) fragility findings测试G-MFRM robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      # Adversarial scenarios\n      scenario_judge_collusion_tau_drop: 0.04\n      scenario_strategic_contamination_tau_drop: 0.06\n      scenario_item_poisoning_tau_drop: 0.03\n      # Comparison: how much do baselines degrade?\n      baseline_sequential_collusion_tau_drop: 0.07\n      baseline_cyclicjudge_collusion_tau_drop: 0.05\n      # Detection\n      gmfrm_detects_collusion_via_d_j_outlier: true\n      gmfrm_detects_strategic_contam_via_c_n_pattern: \"partially\"\n      # Overall\n      gmfrm_more_robust_than_baselines: \"mixed — more robust to judge collusion, similarly vulnerable to strategic contamination\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档下adversarial robustness预期为mixed results。\n      Judge collusion（部分judges协调inflate某模型）：G-MFRM的multi-facet estimation比sequential更robust\n      （Δτ drop 0.04 vs 0.07），因为d_j estimation可以部分absorb coordinated judge behavior。\n      Strategic contamination（模型deliberately leak but hide signals）：G-MFRM与baselines similarly vulnerable\n      （Δτ drop 0.06），因为e_i estimation依赖performance gap，deliberate obfuscation可以defeat this signal。\n      但G-MFRM的diagnostic outputs（d_j outlier detection）提供了detection capability其他方法没有。\n      这是P2 experiment——如果space允许放入paper，主要价值是demonstrates diagnostic use case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S10: Adversarial Robustness\"\n        columns: [\"Scenario\", \"G-MFRM τ Drop\", \"Sequential τ Drop\", \"CyclicJudge τ Drop\", \"G-MFRM Detects?\"]\n        sample_rows:\n          - [\"Judge Collusion (2/8 judges)\", \"−0.04\", \"−0.07\", \"−0.05\", \"Yes (d_j outlier)\"]\n          - [\"Strategic Contamination\", \"−0.06\", \"−0.06\", \"−0.06\", \"Partial (c_n pattern)\"]\n          - [\"Item Poisoning (10% items)\", \"−0.03\", \"−0.04\", \"−0.03\", \"Yes (infit outlier)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S13: τ degradation under each adversarial scenario, comparing methods.\"\n    analysis: >\n      G-MFRM不是adversarially robust的silver bullet，但diagnostic outputs提供了detection capability。\n      Judge collusion detection通过d_j outlier是实际可行的——这是\"judge selection guidance\"贡献的具体体现。\n      Paper中如果include，应framing为\"G-MFRM's diagnostic outputs enable detection of evaluation manipulation\"，\n      而非\"G-MFRM is robust to adversarial attack\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"af9c2bc3-9f18-4e08-9e81-79982f6c114b","total_cost_usd":0.48289675000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12445,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"output_tokens":15689,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15689,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7022,"outputTokens":27,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.007156999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15689,"cacheReadInputTokens":11447,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12445,"webSearchRequests"